eturn any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4184\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2580\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, provide the department name, academic year, the number of subjects offered that are not repeatable for credit and are offered in the fall term, and classify the department as 'HIGH_ACTIVITY' if it offers at least 10% more such subjects than the average across all departments for that year, 'LOW_ACTIVITY' if it offers at least 10% fewer, or 'AVERAGE' otherwise. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3632\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", show the subject title, subject key, offer department name, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, subject ID, academic year, term description, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row, ordered by offer department name and academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2958\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, among subjects that are not repeatable, what is the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by each department? List the academic year, department name, average enrollment, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), ordered by variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2597\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the description of the academic year, the department name, the average total units for all subjects offered by that department in terms that match that academic year and have a term status indicator of 'P', and the deviation of each department's average total units from the overall average total units for that academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3644\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a total of 1 unit, show the subject title from the summary, the course number from the offered table, the subject title from the offered summary, the department name from the summary, the offer department name from the offered summary, the row number within each department name group ordered by subject title from the summary, and for each department, also provide the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student). List the results ordered by department name and row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1023\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year where the Mathematics department has at least one unique subject with subject enrollment number greater than 10, what are the academic year, academic year description, department name, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, variance of total units, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units for subjects offered in the fall term that are not variable units and are offered by the Mathematics department? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
